  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_towelling_diaper_cbd59c355c75df501cee2dee8ab164eafe6670f74c8dbe4fc55fae93386f9af652">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>towel, a cloth, usually of linen or hemp, for wiping something dry, especially for wiping the hands, face, or person after washing or bathing. Also formerly more widely, including a table-napkin or other cloth used at meals (OED s.v. towel n.), made of diaper, a linen fabric (or an inferior fabric of 'union' or cotton) woven with a small and simple pattern, formed by the different directions of the thread, with the different reflexions of light from its surface, and consisting of lines crossing diamond-wise, with the spaces variously filled up by parallel lines, a central leaf or dot, etc. (OED s.v. diaper)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
